    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c043fb5e_596a3b72",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 205,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T09:20:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the implicit assumptions that your code has to deal with are a bit confusing: the `kernel`/`ramdisk`/`memory` ranges don\u0027t need to be validated against the platform assumptions because `MemorySlices` will do so but OTOH device memory ranges (UART and PCI) are NOT validated later and, in the case of PCI, are even [used as-is by pvmfw](http://cs/android/packages/modules/Virtualization/libs/fdtpci/src/lib.rs;l\u003d104;rcl\u003dcdda3967aa9ada05fbac7c0efed291ea72ccdfe0) so need to have been validated beforehand; would `fdt.rs` be the right place to do so? Do we need to extend `MemorySlices` or create an equivalent for devices (knowing that the PCI driver will handle creating the PT entries)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 205,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "6a8789ab3aa6f5ff85b0c31fd0d968836aad0d3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9dc73b4_b0fd0e3e",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 205,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T11:27:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After this stack of changes are applied, any access to fdt even from inside pvmfw will be after the sanitization; PciInfo::from_fdt is called after it, on the sanitized fdt, not the original one.",
      "parentUuid": "c043fb5e_596a3b72",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 205,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "6a8789ab3aa6f5ff85b0c31fd0d968836aad0d3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d54f2471_87036f3c",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 205,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T11:31:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right but is there something that ensures that the PCI range is actually device memory? Because the code that uses it (see link above) doesn\u0027t seem to(?)",
      "parentUuid": "a9dc73b4_b0fd0e3e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 205,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "6a8789ab3aa6f5ff85b0c31fd0d968836aad0d3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6566911b_f844b899",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 205,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T11:56:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Got it. I\u0027ve added another check in a follow-up change. aosp/2508675",
      "parentUuid": "d54f2471_87036f3c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 205,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "6a8789ab3aa6f5ff85b0c31fd0d968836aad0d3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9cfcdc4e_6d55e766",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 309,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T09:20:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "pvmfw might guarantee that UARTs are within device memory or even that they use the PC-standard addresses.\n\nIn particular, this validation is a bit special because pvmfw uses UART `0x3f8` (IIRC) before it starts reading from the DT.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 309,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "6a8789ab3aa6f5ff85b0c31fd0d968836aad0d3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "753ffcc7_3b41cbc8",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 309,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-27T11:27:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The first message is \"pVM firmware\" in main.rs and that is now called after the sanitization is done in entry.rs. Unfortunately, this there\u0027s not check asserting this.\n\nChecking against PC standard address etc is implicitly done during patching; the template DT has four serials with standard addresses, only the devices whose addresses are overlapping between template DT and the input DT survives.",
      "parentUuid": "9cfcdc4e_6d55e766",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 309,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 5
